From 3a52a1b0c569c2129a068fb20c7d6afce42fda2b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shaun Adams <s.adams@f5.com>
Date: Thu, 11 Jun 2026 17:38:38 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] configstore: add TenantRepository CRUD on ConfigStore
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Adds six methods to the ConfigStore interface and implements them on
RDBConfigStore so the platform-admin control plane can manage tenants
without reaching into the DB layer directly:

  GetTenants(ctx)
  GetTenantsPaginated(ctx, params) — search + status filter + paging
  GetTenant(ctx, id)
  CreateTenant(ctx, tenant)
  UpdateTenant(ctx, tenant)
  DeleteTenant(ctx, id)

DeleteTenant is the only non-trivial one:

  - returns ErrReservedTenant for DefaultTenantID — single-tenant OSS
    deployments depend on that row existing
  - returns ErrTenantNotEmpty if any of the 8 tenant-scoped tables
    (customers, teams, virtual_keys, budgets, rate_limits, providers,
    keys, mcp_clients) still holds rows pointing at this tenant_id

Operators wanting "stop billing" semantics should flip Status to
TenantStatusSuspended via UpdateTenant rather than DeleteTenant.

Two new error sentinels in errors.go: ErrTenantNotEmpty and
ErrReservedTenant.

Tests (7 new in rdb_test.go):
  - TestTenant_CreateGetUpdate: round-trip + status flip + rename
  - TestTenant_CreateDuplicateRejected: unique-id enforcement
  - TestTenant_GetNotFound: ErrNotFound on missing id
  - TestTenant_DeleteEmptyTenant: happy-path delete
  - TestTenant_DeleteRefusedWhenNotEmpty: ErrTenantNotEmpty + still
    deletable after dependents are cleaned up
  - TestTenant_DeleteDefaultRefused: ErrReservedTenant on the default
  - TestTenant_ListAndPaginate: list, search by name fragment, status
    filter

setupRDBTestStore also gains TableTenant in its AutoMigrate list and
seeds the default tenant row (the minimal test setup skips the
migration chain that does this for the real DB).

Ref: https://jira.f5net.com/browse/XC-25496
